From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] iio: pressure: Add the Apple AOP barometric pressure sensor

The Always-On Processor of Apple A9 devices samples the barometric
pressure sensor and, once it has the unit's factory calibration and its
batch, raw and report intervals (EPIC set-property tags 0x16, 0x5c and
0), sends one report (EPIC subtype 0xc4) per report interval with the
pressure in 1/65536 kPa.

Expose it as an IIO pressure sensor: raw value, scale in kPa, sampling
frequency (the report interval) and a software buffer with timestamps.
The calibration is complete once the offset or the acceleration
sensitivity is applied; the heater resistance is sent when the
bootloader provides it.

[Orchard: from orchard PR #101, commit a54e2049; the pressure part of
 drivers/iio/0005, unchanged]

Assisted-by: LLM
